before:
isset($items["score"]) is false for missing or null values. array_key_exists("score", $items) checks whether the key exists even if its value is null.

isset checks whether the supplied entry is both present and non-null. array_key_exists receives a key and array and tests key presence even when the stored value is null. Both return Booleans; neither modifies the array. This concrete comparison keeps a present zero distinct from null.
```php
<?php
$items = ["score" => null];
var_export(isset($items["score"])); echo "\n";
var_export(array_key_exists("score", $items)); echo "\n";
$items["score"] = 0;
var_export(isset($items["score"])); echo "\n";
```
Expected output: false; true; true.

